    "reviewTitle": "Soft and Fits Small Ears, But Watch the Slow Expansion (Video Included)",
    "reviewDescription": "These are definitely sized well for small ear canals, and the foam material is very soft. I uploaded a photo comparing these to standard earplugs so you can see the size difference. The Application: One thing to note is that after you roll them down, they take an extremely long time to expand back to their original size. Check out the clip I attached; you can see just how long you have to wait for them to fill the space and seal the ear canal. Design Concern: My main worry is the shape. Because they are roughly the same width all the way through (no flared base or stopper), I am always careful not to push them in too far.",
